# Curated to what this tree actually produces: .NET build output and test
# runs, the Rust crate's cargo target, the operator UI's node and bundle
# output, the teamserver's local data directory, and editor/OS noise.

# .NET build output and test runs
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
artifacts/
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info

# Rust implant tree: each crate root's cargo build output (target/ holds the
# compiled binaries and the generated protobuf bindings under
# target/release/build). The checked-in
# baked.rs stub is tracked (empty -- the build unit overwrites it in a temp
# copy at build time); the loader crate beside it follows the same rule.
src/implant/rust/target/
src/implant/rust/loader/target/
src/implant/rust/plugin-sdk/target/
src/implant/rust/modules/*/target/
src/implant/rust/carrier/target/

# The plugin packages' build and publish output (modules/*/): build.sh
# copies the cargo-built binary into plugin/ before a publish, and rod mod
# publish defaults its --out to dist/ -- the artifact rides signed
# packages, never the tree.
modules/*/plugin/
modules/*/dist/

# Operator UI: the Vite build output is produced by `npm run build` (CI does it
# before `dotnet build`); only the React sources under src/teamserver/Rod.TeamServer/Client
# are tracked, not the emitted wwwroot bundle.
src/teamserver/Rod.TeamServer/wwwroot/
node_modules/

# Runtime state the teamserver writes when Audit:DataDirectory points at a
# local directory (a dev-loop shape): the file-backed trail and blobs are
# per-install state, never source.
src/teamserver/Rod.TeamServer/data/

# Local configuration
.env

# Agent session state (tooling working directory, never source)
.zcode/

# Editor state
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.user
*.suo
*.rsuser

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
[Dd]esktop.ini

# Logs
*.log

# Docs site build output (mkdocs, docs-site.yml): the site renders the
# tracked files, and the derived home page (docs/index.md, from README.md)
# is a build artifact, never committed.
site/
docs/index.md
